        "type": "Module",
        "name": "preamplifier",
        "description": "NE5532 dual op-amp used as the low-level preamplifier stage powered from the external single 9V rail and GND. This module accepts the external audio input, applies the main voltage gain shaping needed to reach the overall target gain together with the LM386 stage, and drives the LM386 input through an interstage analog path. Because only one preamplifier channel is required by the brief, one amplifier section is planned as the active gain stage and the second section remains available for bias buffering, input conditioning, or stability-related support if needed during downstream design; no unsupported pin assumptions are made. Single-supply operation requires downstream biasing and signal-centering networks to be implemented around the available input and output pins rather than assuming split supplies.",
