        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_amplifier",
        "description": "LM386 low-voltage audio power amplifier used as the final speaker driver stage powered from the external single 9V rail and GND. This module receives the preamplified analog signal from the NE5532, provides the final power gain needed to drive the 8-ohm speaker, and exposes the speaker output as the board-level load interface. Gain-setting intent must use the provided GAIN_1 and GAIN_2 pins if higher LM386 gain is required to meet the overall 100x-200x target in combination with the preamplifier stage. IN_NEG should be configured according to the intended single-ended input topology during downstream wiring, and BYPASS may be used for supply-noise and bias stabilization if needed. The speaker is a high-current load on this module output, so downstream design should keep the power output return path distinct from the low-level preamp signal routing even though both share common GND.",
